WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.580
Hey, welcome to Tesla Short's Time, Daily Episode 517. Patrick here in Vancouver,

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:11.500
it's June 21st, 2026. Here's your Tesla news rundown. The week's biggest developments

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:15.780
pulled together, what actually moved, why it matters, and what to watch next.

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:22.260
Danish regulators approved Tesla's supervised, full-self-driving package for public roads this week.

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:28.240
The clearance came after local testing and adds another European Union market for the feature.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:33.940
At the same time, legal action in Europe over marketing claims versus delivered performance

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:39.200
is moving forward. The case centers on statements about full-self-driving capabilities

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:42.620
compared with what the system actually provides in those markets.

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:50.040
Fresh reports also showed supervised FSD avoiding animals on roads and completing door-to-door

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:57.420
trips without driver intervention in tested scenarios. Remember, the show last covered FSD unsupervised

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:04.400
on Episode 516, and this approval moves the supervised expansion forward while the regulatory

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:11.260
path for unsupervised operation stays the main open question. Attentive listeners will watch whether

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:17.480
other Nordic countries follow Denmark's lead in the coming weeks. Upcoming FSD releases will add

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:23.580
GROC voice control and stored parking preferences. The system will recall prior parking locations and

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:30.080
without new driver input. These features aim to reduce repeated manual steps in familiar settings.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:34.620
Development ties into broader software updates for the supervised stack.

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:43.320
Owners can expect the changes in a future software branch. FSD V14.3.4 specifically avoided a

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:49.260
squirrel in one documented clip. Separate reports showed the system preventing side swipes in a

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:56.540
dangerous situation. FSD supervised enables door-to-door autonomous driving in additional tested cases.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:01.920
Tesla FSD saves animal lives appeared in multiple fresh clips this week.

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:10.860
On the product side, the lowest priced cyber truck trim at $59,990 began reaching early owners

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:17.400
this week. The variant trims range and features compared with higher trims but expands the line-up for

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:24.540
more buyers. Tesla is also validating a longer wheelbase Model Y for potential US production

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:31.960
while cyber truck volume grows. A slightly stretched Model Y variant was photographed on roads in San

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:40.080
Jose. The Model Y L is currently built only at gigafactory Shanghai and the sighting points to early US

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:46.900
validation work. Elon Musk had indicated a possible year end US arrival, though he called the timing

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:54.200
uncertain. This connects to the ongoing next-gen vehicle program last reviewed on Episode 515,

00:02:54.740 --> 00:03:00.800
where cost reduction targets remain the central open question. Hardware updates like the Model Y,

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:07.920
L sit alongside deeper software and training infrastructure work inside Tesla. Tesla filed new

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:14.120
patents aimed at improving dojo training efficiency on imperfect ethernet networks. One patent uses

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:20.420
on chip cache and linked lists to retransmit only missing segments instead of restarting entire

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:27.320
streams. The second patent moves flow control and acknowledgments into a custom Mac block for faster

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:33.100
hardware managed links. These changes target higher training throughput for both full self-driving

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:41.380
and optimist development. Remember the show last covered HW1 and Dojo on Episode 513 and these

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:46.560
filings address the production timeline and scaling questions still open for the next generation

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:56.500
hardware. Tesla's W02024-039800 patent describes a micro architecture that stores recent packets

00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:04.900
in on chip cache or SRAM as small as 256 kilobytes and uses linked lists to track transmission order.

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:11.280
When an acknowledgement fails or a timer expires, hardware pointers identify only the missing

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:17.640
segment for replay instead of restarting the stream. Four pipeline stages handle stream selection,

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:23.820
link identification, replay or retire decisions, and pointer updates without software intervention.

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:30.320
A hardware link timer working with FIFO memory checks multiple links in round robin fashion and

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:36.920
adapts its tick period as the number of active links changes. This approach keeps dojo training throughput

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:48.000
high, even on a controlled but imperfect ethernet fabric. Tesla's W02024-039794 patent moves transport

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:55.140
layer functions including flow control, acknowledgments, and replay into a TTP Mac block that operates

00:04:55.140 --> 00:05:03.660
across OSI layers two to four. Frames carry a specific ether type such as 0x9AC6. So standard

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:10.300
ethernet switches can forward them while TTP endpoints manage state in hardware. Link state

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:16.780
machines transition through closed, open-send, open-received, open-close-send, and closed-received

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:23.680
without TCP style time-weight periods. Bounded packet transmission plus local storage supports

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:32.540
the design. Tesla's suspension patent builds on 1,998 Lincoln Mark 8 tech. Tesla's new design pairs

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:39.100
low-rate parallel air springs with series dampers for most ride duties. The active actuator only

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:45.020
corrects when needed, cutting energy use compared with fully active systems. The approach draws from

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:52.600
the 1,998 Lincoln Mark 8's air suspension but adds passive dominant tuning. This could help preserve

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:58.800
range on vehicles that already carry heavy battery packs. Starlink ran advertisements during the UFC

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:06.060
Freedom 250 broadcast on Paramount Plus. The placement reached a large live sports audience and

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:13.100
overlaps with Tesla's brand exposure through shared SpaceX channels. Wedbush analyst Dan Ives released

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:20.200
a note calling SpaceX's IPO pricing a Goldilocks outcome that avoided draining capital from the broader

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:27.320
tech trade. Ives pointed to continued AI infrastructure spending and named Palantir, Snowflake,

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:34.040
and Datadog as beneficiaries. President Trump confirmed Starlink will equip the next Air Force one.

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:41.420
The boring company commissioned its second proof-frock machine, proof-frock MB2 for the music city loop

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:47.840
in Nashville. The addition doubles tunneling capacity for the project. Work continues on the

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:54.040
initial airport area segment. South Korea let an EV purchase tax incentive expire,

00:06:54.040 --> 00:07:00.320
raising prices for most models. Tesla vehicles retain favorable treatment under existing

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:06.740
rules, creating a relative price advantage. Local analysts expect the shift to steer some buyers

00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:13.360
toward Tesla in the second half of the year. Tesla and Ford engineers disassembled Chinese market

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:18.540
EVs to study battery integration and assembly methods that lower production expenses.

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:23.340
The findings are feeding into both companies' own cost reduction programs.

00:07:23.740 --> 00:07:29.820
This competitive analysis work echoes Tesla's ongoing efforts at home to match or beat overseas

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:36.400
manufacturing approaches. Chinese firm Hina battery has developed sodium ion cells whose energy

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:42.960
density is nearing levels seen in current Tesla packs. The chemistry offers potential cost and supply

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:49.060
chain advantages over lithium-based systems. No deployment timeline with Tesla has been disclosed.

00:07:49.720 --> 00:07:55.820
Tesla locks down amazing abundance, trademarks spanning robotics, AI chips and robotaxi.

00:07:56.360 --> 00:08:00.760
The trademark filing covers multiple future product categories in one action.

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:06.740
Now one thing worth watching is the advancing legal case in Europe over full self-driving

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:12.180
marketing claims. The action focuses on the gap between advertised performance and what

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:18.660
supervised systems currently deliver in those markets. While regulatory approvals like Denmark's

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:24.860
expand supervised access, the case highlights the risk that overstated claims could slow broader

00:08:24.860 --> 00:08:31.300
acceptance. Tesla's position rests on continued data collection and software iteration to close that

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:38.500
gap over time. The patents on Dojo hardware replay and TTPOE links break down a core training

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:44.620
bottleneck. Standard ethernet can drop packets forcing full restarts that waste compute cycles.

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:50.560
By handling retransmission and flow control and hardware with small caches and custom state

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:56.960
machines, the designs keep pipelines moving without software overhead. This matters because Dojo

00:08:56.960 --> 00:09:01.800
throughput directly affects how quickly new full self-driving and optimist models improve.

00:09:02.460 --> 00:09:07.700
The open question remains how soon these gains translate into measurable training speed increases

00:09:07.700 --> 00:09:14.080
at scale. Before we go, keep an eye on whether additional European regulators followed Denmark's

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:21.240
supervised FSD approval in the next few weeks. That's your Tesla news for today. TSLA closed

